  "Question": "Casey’s shop class is making a golf trophy. He has to paint \\(300\\) dimples on a golf ball. If it takes him \\(2\\) seconds to paint one dimple, how many minutes will he need to do his job?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(8\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Each of the \\(300\\) dimples takes \\(2\\) seconds, so the total painting time is\n\\[\n300\\cdot2=600\\text{ seconds}.\n\\]\nSince one minute contains \\(60\\) seconds, this is\n\\[\n600\\div60=\\boxed{10\\text{ minutes}},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
